CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ both invoked: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The first call's specialization has a one-element pack, whose parameter
a2 was put into invoke's template scope as a plain parameter symbol of
type int.  For the second call that symbol hid the two-element pack in the
trailing return type, so static_cast<S &>(a2) was checked against an int
and the call had no candidate.
